Download quarto.code-snippets
To install them by hand: Command Palette → Snippets: Configure Snippets → pick quarto (for quarto.json) or New Global Snippets file (for quarto.code-snippets), then paste the content. On disk they live in the profile’s snippets/ folder (%APPDATA%\Code\User\profiles\&lt;profile id&gt;\snippets\).

Tasks
Run a task with Command Palette → Tasks: Run Task, or with its keybinding.









Task
Keybinding
Script
What it does




Git: Return to updated main
Ctrl+Alt+Shift+M
return-to-main.ps1
After a PR is merged, gets you onto an up-to-date main with one checkout (details below).


R: New scratch project
none
new-r-scratch-project.ps1
Asks for a name, creates an RStudio-style R project in Documents\R-scratch\&lt;name&gt; with usethis::create_project(), and opens it in a new VS Code window.



Both are "type": "process" tasks that start pwsh -NoProfile -File "${env:USERPROFILE}/.vscode-scripts/&lt;script&gt;.ps1". Using ${env:USERPROFILE} keeps tasks.json free of user names, so the file works on any machine.

Git: Return to updated main
The usual way back after a large PR is merged (git switch main, then git pull) updates the working tree twice: first to the old main, then to the new one. On a big repository both steps are slow.
The script avoids the first one:

Stops if there are uncommitted changes.
Finds the remote’s default branch (main, master, …).
Fetches only that branch (git fetch --no-tags origin main).
Moves the local main to the fetched commit without checking it out (git update-ref, only if it is a fast-forward).
Checks out main once, straight into the new state.
Deletes the branch you came from with git branch -d, which only succeeds when git sees it as merged into main or identical to what was pushed. Otherwise it tells you and keeps the branch.

If you are already on main, it just fast-forwards (git merge --ff-only).


R: New scratch project
For quick experiments that deserve their own folder but not a repository.

Rscript is taken from PATH, i.e. rig’s default R version (rig default &lt;version&gt;). Pass -RScriptPath to use another one.
Needs the usethis package in the default R version (it comes with devtools).
The task input rScratchProjectName is a promptString: VS Code asks for the name when the task starts.



